<pre>
<code>
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Concourse entrypoint for build-windows-stemcell.
set -euo pipefail
SCRIPT_DIR=$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" &> /dev/null && pwd)
WINDOWS_DIR="${SCRIPT_DIR}/windows-automation"
# Verifies packer, govc, and at least one stembuild binary (stembuild-2019, stembuild-2022, etc.)
# Builds variables.pkrvars.hcl from Concourse params (vcenter_*, ISO_PATH or TEMPLATE_PATH, network, ...).
# Downloads Packer vSphere plugin, runs: packer init windows-vm.pkr.hcl
# Runs: ./build.sh -v variables.pkrvars.hcl [ --jumper-ip ... ]
pushd "$WINDOWS_DIR"
# ... generate VARS_FILE, packer init ...
./build.sh -v "$VARS_FILE" "${BUILD_ARGS[@]}" "${JUMPER_ARGS[@]}"
mkdir -p "$OLD_PWD/logs"
cp -r logs/* "$OLD_PWD/logs" 2>/dev/null || true
STEMCELL_FILE=$(find . -name "bosh-stemcell-*-vsphere-esxi-*-go_agent.tgz" -type f 2>/dev/null | head -1)
if [[ -n "$STEMCELL_FILE" ]]; then
  mkdir -p "$OLD_PWD/stemcell"
  cp "$STEMCELL_FILE" "$OLD_PWD/stemcell"
fi
popd

</code>
</pre>

<p class="note">
The script runs from the <code>windows-automation</code> directory next to <code>build-windows-stemcell.sh</code>.
It writes <code>variables.pkrvars.hcl</code>, initializes Packer, invokes <code>build.sh</code>, then copies <code>logs/</code> and the stemcell <code>.tgz</code> into the Concourse task output directories.
</p>
